# Copy to worker/.dev.vars for `wrangler dev` (gitignored, never commit real values).
# In production these are set as Worker secrets instead — see README.md's
# "Remote deployment" section — either via `wrangler secret put` or, when the
# Worker is connected to this repo through Workers Builds, under the Worker's
# Settings > Variables & Secrets in the Cloudflare dashboard.
#
# Single-tenant (default) — one deployment, one YNAB account, gated by a
# shared secret:
YNAB_API_KEY=replace-with-your-ynab-personal-access-token
MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-token

# Multi-tenant instead — lets other people use this deployment with their own
# YNAB accounts (each caller's own token travels with their request, so no
# YNAB_API_KEY/MCP_AUTH_TOKEN needed at all). Uncomment this and remove the
# two lines above:
# MCP_MULTI_TENANT=true
